  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s20/50572166> ;
  triage:notes "Followup pass: s18-s20 retain original inline match duplication pattern; s21-s25 have been refactored (s21's collapse-dispatch-routing sprint) to use shared helper functions (into_send_outcome, into_ack_outcome) from atm-core::protocol module. Caller-side duplication eliminated in s21+, but library-level duplication of the two helper functions persists (tracked separately as RBQA-F011 meta-finding about missing lint gate for this pattern class). Dispatch targets s20 (highest open branch); fix should consolidate s18-s20 lineage to match s21+ refactored pattern using protocol helpers, OR conversely, extract a shared From/TryFrom trait to handle both Sent and Acknowledged outcomes in one place. Both approaches eliminate the caller-side duplication present in s18-s20." .

